A||||5||Cheever3000||What's different since Sept. 11th?||||2||
Z||000000||Cheever3000||12-04-2001||11:54 PM||||Planes <I>seem</I> to be flying lower.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><P>Firefighters seem taller.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>And there definitely seem to be more deformed M&M's.  I think I know where those darn terrorist infiltrators are: working at the M&M factory!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif"><P>What's <B>not</B> different is my creditors haven't gotten the word that they're supposed to let me skip a few payments.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><BR>||||reg||2
Z||000001||California Kid||12-05-2001||12:12 AM||||One hell of a lot of people laid off in the Metro Detroit Area!!! The Big 3 Auto Makers ruined Christmas for a large part of it's work force, and they're still cutting more this month.<P>Hate to say this, but we're slipping into a recession!!!  Just my opinion, I was through the bad times in the mid 70's, again in mid to late 80's, but it wasn't as scary as what we're headed into right now.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Nashco||12-05-2001||01:12 AM||||What's different?  Well, my bank account is still empty...I don't know if this means I'm spending like the man says I'm supposed to, or if I'm just not making any <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Also killer gas prices lately (saw 83 cents in Atlanta last weekend), I think something fishy is going on.<P>Lastly, airline ticket prices haven't gone down hardly at all compared to any other time I've bought tickets...I figured they would do to less people flying and lower fuel costs, but I guess that there are other things counter-balancing it.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000003||deceler8||12-05-2001||09:36 AM||||Don't take as much for granted as I used to.<P>I have more appreciation for leadership and the military in this country and I'd love to shake the hands of some Northern Alliance fighters who have really done a lot of our dirty work for us and in the process saved lots of American lives.<P>Even in the midst of this recession, this is still the greatest place in the world to live by a factor of about a million.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Jefrysuko||12-05-2001||10:27 AM||||Letterman has stopped touching his toes at the beginning of his show each day.||||reg||1
Z||000005||fogglethorpe||12-05-2001||06:39 PM||||Now we know that America is vulnerable instead of invincible. (Yes, a shameless plug for missile defense)<P>I have a deeper appreciation for firefighters, police officers, rescue workers, and especially our military.<P>I realize that George W. Bush is a decent man of integrity, whose gift of leadership has greatly emerged in a crisis.<P>I worry more about what kind of world my children will inherit.<P>God bless the USA, greatest country in the history of the world!||||reg||1
